    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** (62.21) serving as our premier start. His matchup against Nola offers a favorable park adjustment and, while he faces a slight penalty for the pitcher's efficiency at holding runners, his elite profile in a high-leverage spot makes him our most bankable asset. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.57) and **Kyle Tucker** (61.21) follow closely as the engine of our offensive production; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a significant boost due to his premium slot in the #3 hole and a favorable matchup against Elder, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a \"Strong\" play despite Soroka\u2019s presence, buoyed by the stability of his base projections.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary catalyst for our roster construction today, most notably for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (60.31). His score is heavily inflated by a +14% dynamic platoon advantage against Bachar, allowing him to outperform several higher-base-projection teammates. Conversely, we are mitigating risk by tempering expectations for **Gunnar Henderson** (50.05); despite his elite talent, he faces a significant -15% drag due to both the SP skill and the platoon disadvantage against Early. The most difficult decision on the bench was **Coby Mayo** (47.33); he was the final cut, narrowly missing the starting nine because his efficiency profile against Early did not provide the same upside as our current middle-infield starters, despite the park factors favoring him. We remain cautious regarding **Liam Hicks** (43.85), whose value is constrained by a difficult matchup against Lovelady, but we are keeping him in the lineup to maintain our game cap discipline. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains our most significant inactive, and we are monitoring for any late-breaking weather or lineup changes that might force an adjustment for our fringe starters.",
